; tools/lispm-check's self-test, run with --files selftest.lisp.
; Three cases fail on purpose: one expected value is wrong, one error's message
; is not the one expected, and one form signals an error it was not marked for. The self-test (run.sh) checks each verdict
; and the exit status 1.

; passing cases: a value compared, a value printed, a form over two lines
(check-selftest-square 7) => 49
(+ 1 2)
(list 'a
      (check-selftest-square 3)) => (A 9)
"a string" => "a string"

; a deliberately failing case: the expected value is wrong
(check-selftest-square 4) => 17

; expected errors: any error, and one whose message must contain a text
(car 1) =>!
(check-selftest-fail 3) =>! Self-test error with 3

; a deliberately failing case: an error, but not with the expected message
(check-selftest-fail 4) =>! Self-test error with 5

; an unexpected error
(check-selftest-undefined 1)

; the listener is still there after the errors
(check-selftest-square 5) => 25
